{{!-- A1, "List", on an author archive: the centred profile over the shared row.

	{{> "author/a1"}}

The author archive shares the Feed's `feed_layout` setting for the same reason the tag archive
does: a buyer picking "a wide row per post" meant it wherever posts are listed. It now shares the
ROW too — `archive/list-row.hbs`, the Feed's — rather than the compact row the design drew here.
One setting that draws three different rows is three drawings a publication cannot choose between.

That row carries the writer's face and name on every post, which on this Surface is the same face
and the same name each time. The repetition is the price of one row everywhere, and it is the
cheaper side of the trade: the compact row's whole reason for existing was to reorder two meta
facts.

No lead story on this Surface in either layout. The design draws one on the tag archive and none
here, and a writer's page is a body of work rather than a front page.

PAGE WIDTH, not the design's 1120px column, so the rows are the Feed's rows exactly. The profile
above them keeps its own narrower measure — see author/header.hbs. --}}
{{#with author}}
	{{> "author/header" total=../pagination.total}}
{{/with}}

<section
	id="posts"
	aria-label="{{t "Posts"}}"
	class="border-border container border-t">
	{{#foreach posts}}
		{{> "archive/list-row"}}
	{{else}}
		<p class="font-body text-muted py-11">{{t "No posts by this writer yet."}}</p>
	{{/foreach}}
</section>
